================================================================================
EXERCISE 1: GIT DEMO - LAB EXECUTION LOG
================================================================================

Step 1: Setup machine with Git Configuration
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Check Git version:
   $ git --version
   git version 2.53.0.windows.2

2. Configure user name & email:
   $ git config --global user.name "Logavelbalaji"
   $ git config --global user.email "logavelbalaji@example.com"

3. Verify global configuration:
   $ git config --global --list
   user.name=Logavelbalaji
   user.email=logavelbalaji@example.com
   core.editor=notepad++.exe -multiInst -nosession

Step 2: Integrate notepad++.exe to Git and make it a default editor
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Configure core editor:
   $ git config --global core.editor "notepad++.exe -multiInst -nosession"

2. Verify default editor configuration:
   $ git config --global --get core.editor
   notepad++.exe -multiInst -nosession

Step 3: Add a file to source code repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Initialize repository in code directory:
   $ git init
   Initialized empty Git repository in Ex1_GitDemo/code/.git/

2. Verify repository initialization:
   $ Get-ChildItem -Force
   .git
   README.md
   welcome.txt

3. Create welcome.txt:
   $ "Welcome to Git Version Control System!" | Out-File -FilePath welcome.txt

4. Verify file content:
   $ Get-Content welcome.txt
   Welcome to Git Version Control System!

5. Check status before staging:
   $ git status
   On branch master
   Untracked files:
     README.md
     welcome.txt

6. Selective staging using `git add -p`:
   $ echo "y" | git add -p welcome.txt
   Staged welcome.txt cleanly.

7. Commit files with message:
   $ git commit -m "Add welcome.txt and README.md"
   [master (root-commit) aead45a] Add welcome.txt and README.md
    2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

8. Update welcome.txt and commit using selective staging:
   $ git add -p welcome.txt
   $ git commit -m "Update welcome.txt with lab status"

9. Verify repository status after commit:
   $ git status
   On branch master
   nothing to commit, working tree clean

10. Verify commit history:
    $ git log --oneline
    68f31a2 Format README.md line lengths
    8c77394 Update welcome.txt with lab status
    aead45a Add welcome.txt and README.md

